-- 4. the refusals, each beside the case it must accept
ok 4a.1 ACCEPTED: a language tag with a hyphen
ok 4a.2 a space is not a language tag
ok 4a.3 and neither is nothing
ok 4b.1 ACCEPTED: letters, digits, '-' and '_'
ok 4b.2 an id may not start with a digit
ok 4b.3 an id that would end the attribute is refused
ok 4c.1 ACCEPTED: another path on this origin
ok 4c.2 ACCEPTED: a CDN, because HeaderOptions exists to allow one
ok 4c.3 a javascript: src is refused
ok 4c.4 and the check is not fooled by case
ok 4c.5 a data: src is refused
ok 4c.6 a quote would end the attribute and start another
ok 4c.6b and a space splits the value in two
ok 4c.7 an empty src is refused
ok 4c.8 ACCEPTED: two stylesheets
ok 4c.9 and the message names WHICH one
ok 4d.1 ACCEPTED: an absolute path
ok 4d.2 an absolute URL is refused
ok 4d.3 and so is a protocol-relative one
ok 4d.4 and so is a relative one
ok 4e.1 ACCEPTED: exactly the 16 characters CircuitSet.open needs
ok 4e.2 one character fewer is an id no socket can use
ok 4e.3 and a character that would end the attribute is refused
ok 4e.4 an id on a page that says it wants no circuit is a contradiction
ok 4f.1 render_shell refuses what faults() names
ok 4f.2 and emits nothing at all
ok 4f.3 ACCEPTED: the same options with the URL made a path

